# ⚡ 2. Important Commands You Used (REAL DEVOPS TOOLS)

## 🔍 Search inside project (VERY IMPORTANT)

```bash
grep -R "localhost:5112" .
```

👉 Finds hardcoded bad config across whole project

---

```bash
grep -R "/api/" wwwroot/js
```

👉 Checks frontend API usage

---

```bash
grep -R "const API" .
```

👉 Finds duplicated or conflicting frontend configs

---

## 📁 Find duplicate files (CRITICAL in real systems)

```bash
find . -name "admin.js"
```

👉 Detects multiple versions of same file (VERY common bug)

---

## 📄 Inspect file content quickly

```bash
cat wwwroot/js/admin.js | head -5
```

👉 Verifies what is ACTUALLY deployed

---

## 🔄 Restart backend properly

```bash
pkill dotnet
dotnet clean
dotnet build
dotnet run
```

👉 This fixes:

* stale builds
* cached DLLs
* old runtime state

---

## 🌐 Test server directly (VERY IMPORTANT DEVOPS SKILL)

```bash
curl http://192.168.1.9:5000/js/admin.js
```

👉 Bypasses browser completely
👉 Shows real server output

---

## 📂 Check static files exist

```bash
ls wwwroot/images/I/
```

or

```bash
find wwwroot/images -type f
```

👉 Confirms if files exist on server

---

## 🧪 Test API directly

```bash
curl http://192.168.1.9:5000/api/Products
```

👉 Removes frontend from equation

---

## 🧹 Remove build artifacts (VERY IMPORTANT)

```bash
rm -rf bin obj
```

👉 Forces clean rebuild (fixes ghost bugs)

---

# ⚙️ 3. ASP.NET Core DevOps Concepts You Used

## 🌍 Binding to network (CRITICAL)

```csharp
app.WebHost.UseUrls("http://0.0.0.0:5000");
```

👉 Means:

* localhost = only your machine ❌
* 0.0.0.0 = accessible from LAN ✔

---

## 📁 Static files

```csharp
app.UseStaticFiles();
```

👉 Enables:

* `/wwwroot/js`
* `/wwwroot/images`
* `/wwwroot/css`

---

## 🔐 CORS policy (important for APIs)

```csharp
.AllowAnyOrigin()
.AllowAnyMethod()
.AllowAnyHeader();
```

👉 Allows frontend on other devices to access backend

